<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/2nd-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Myonessus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">190 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/2nd-century-bce">2nd century BCE</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-seleucid-war">Roman–Seleucid War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Myonessus was a naval battle fought off the coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ionia">Ionia</a> in 190 BCE, in which a Roman and Rhodian fleet under Lucius Aemilius Regillus defeated the Seleucid fleet commanded by Polyxenidas. The victory gave the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a> control of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aegean">Aegean</a> and allowed their army to cross into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia-minor">Asia Minor</a>, where it defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antiochus-iii-the-great">Antiochus III</a> at Magnesia.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-myonessus.jpg" alt="Battle of Myonessus" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Matt Boulton · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rhodian_Trireme.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
